 🧾 Invoice vs Bill – Easy Terms
🔹 Term	Invoice	Bill

Who sends it?	        A seller or service provider	    A buyer or business receiving it
Who receives it?	    A customer or client	            The business owner (you)
Purpose	To request      payment for goods/services	        To record money you owe to someone else

🧠 Quick Way to Remember:
Invoice = Money you expect to RECEIVE.


Bill = Money you need to PAY.
