📌 Project Objective:
Build a secure, automated solution to extract transaction data from Xero (4 companies) and import it into an Azure SQL Server database, running autonomously on an Azure Virtual Machine (no third-party cloud use).

✅ Key Responsibilities:
# Xero API Integration:

    Connect securely to Xero for 4 companies.

    Extract  Invoices (Sales & Purchases), payments, and bank transactions.

    Handle access token management,Data Transformation & Mapping and ensure complete data retrieval.

# Data Transformation & Mapping:

    The data should be stored in the SQL server in a format that is appropriate for reporting.

    necessary data transformations should be handled (e.g., date format conversions, currency handling, data type adjustments) 
    to align with the Azure SQL schema and ensure consistency for reporting.  

    Add processTimestamp to each record.

    Gracefully handle missing or inconsistent data.

# Azure SQL Server Integration:

    Securely connect to existing database.

    Use upsert logic to insert/update data.

    Optimize for bulk loading performance.

# Automation & Scheduling:

    Automate weekly data imports from Xero Application to their SQL Server DATABASE.

    Run as a scheduled task on the Azure VM.

# Error Handling & Logging:

    Implement robust logging and error reporting for Api failures,data Transformation issues and any other error.

    Optional email alerts for critical issues.

# Security & Best Practices:

    Securely store credentials (Azure Key Vault if possible).

    Maintain clean, well-documented, and maintainable code.


